# PROJECT: APAAR SETU – AICTE STUDENT DATA MANAGEMENT & VERIFICATION PLATFORM

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, database architect, cybersecurity engineer and AI application developer.

Build a complete, professional, modern, responsive and functional full-stack web application named:

**APAAR SETU**
**Tagline: One ID. One Seat. One Verified Truth.**

This is a Smart India Hackathon 2026 project based on the problem statement:

**SIH Problem Statement ID: SIH26263**

Problem Statement Title:
Development of an APAAR ID-based Student Data Management and Verification Platform for AICTE-Approved Institutions.

The objective is to develop a centralized digital platform through which AICTE-approved institutions can upload, update, validate and monitor student-level admission information using APAAR ID as the unique academic identifier.

The application must demonstrate how student records can be securely submitted by institutions, validated automatically, stored in a central repository, monitored by AICTE and verified by authorized stakeholders.

IMPORTANT:
Do not create only a static UI or landing page. Build a fully functional, interactive prototype with working navigation, dashboards, forms, data tables, validation logic, charts, role-based interfaces, QR generation and verification.

The application must be suitable for demonstrating in front of Smart India Hackathon judges.

