- View registered students.
- Monitor approved intake.
- Monitor actual enrolment.
- See available seats.
- View supernumerary seat information.
- Review validation errors.
- Resolve data inconsistencies.
- Generate student reports.
- Generate student verification credentials.

An institution must only be allowed to access its own records.

## C. STUDENT

This user can:
- View their student profile.
- View their APAAR ID status.
- View institution and programme information.
- View admission details.
- View generated student credentials.
- View their QR code.
- Give consent to authorized verification requests.
- Revoke consent.
- View their verification history.

## D. EMPLOYER / AUTHORIZED VERIFIER

This user can:
- Enter a student credential ID.
- Scan or upload a QR code.
- Verify digitally signed student credentials.
- Check whether the credential is valid.
- View only permitted information.
- View the institution and programme information.
- View verification status.

The verifier must not have access to the full student database.

Implement server-side role and institution-level authorization. Hiding a button in the frontend is not sufficient security.

